{"abstract":"Engaging in the deliberate generation of abnormal outputs from Large Language Models (LLMs) by attacking them is a novel human activity. This paper presents a thorough exposition of how and why people perform such attacks, defining LLM red-teaming based on extensive and diverse evidence. Using a formal qualitative methodology, we interviewed dozens of practitioners from a broad range of backgrounds, all contributors to this novel work of attempting to cause LLMs to fail. We focused on the research questions of defining LLM red teaming, uncovering the motivations and goals for performing the activity, and characterizing the strategies people use when attacking LLMs. Based on the data, LLM red teaming is defined as a limit-seeking, non-malicious, manual activity, which depends highly on a team-effort and an alchemist mindset. It is highly intrinsically motivated by curiosity, fun, and to some degrees by concerns for various harms of deploying LLMs. We identify a taxonomy of 12 strategies and 35 different techniques of attacking LLMs. These findings are presented as a comprehensive grounded theory of how and why people attack large language models: LLM red teaming.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Derczynski, Leon","Stray, Jonathan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798542"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NVIDIA","University of California, Berkeley","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Large Language Models","Qualitative methodology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"summon a demon and bind it a grounded theory of llm red teaming","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0314658","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798542","identifier":[{"id":"85215128727","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-820a9387-38ad-4056-93ca-7d24d10a4111"],"keyword":["Abnormal output generation","LLM red-teaming","Large Language Models","Limit-seeking strategies","Qualitative methodology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1A033932B4C58A09AF7F27EB4476520D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0314658","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"nvidia","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NVIDIA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of california berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California, Berkeley","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan","key":"straypau","last":"Stray","name":"Stray, Jonathan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0314658","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"1","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0314658","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215128727"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-820a9387-38ad-4056-93ca-7d24d10a4111"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Summon a demon and bind it: A grounded theory of LLM red teaming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798542","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"As NLP models are used by a growing number of end-users, an area of increasing importance is NLP Security (NLPSec): assessing the vulnerability of models to malicious attacks and developing comprehensive countermeasures against them. While work at the intersection of NLP and cybersecurity has the potential to create safer NLP for all, accidental oversights can result in tangible harm (e.g., breaches of privacy or proliferation of malicious models). In this emerging field, however, the research ethics of NLP have not yet faced many of the long-standing conundrums pertinent to cybersecurity, until now. We thus examine contemporary works across NLPSec, and explore their engagement with cybersecurity's ethical norms. We identify trends across the literature, ultimately finding alarming gaps on topics like harm minimization and responsible disclosure. To alleviate these concerns, we provide concrete recommendations to help NLP researchers navigate this space more ethically, bridging the gap between traditional cybersecurity and NLP ethics, which we frame as \"white hat NLP\". The goal of this work is to help cultivate an intentional culture of ethical research for those working in NLP Security.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lent, Heather","Galinkin, Erick","Chen, Yiyi","Pedersen, Jens Myrup","Derczynski, Leon","Bjerva, Johannes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805260"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NVIDIA"],"keyword":["AI ethics","Cybersecurity","Ethics","LLM Security","LLMsec","NLP","NLP Security","NLPsec","Natural Language Processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nlp security and ethics in the wild","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/tacl_a_00762","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["H. L., Y. C., and J. B. are funded by the Carlsberg Foundation, under the Semper Ardens: Accelerate programme (project nr. CF21-0454). This work benefited greatly from help and conversations with others. Thank you to Christopher Fiorelli and Maria Antoniak at AI2 for their help with the Semantic Scholar crawler, to Zeerak Talat for detailed feedback on our manuscript, and to Steven Bird for conversations on ethics of AI, which enriched this manuscript. Thank you to members of the AAU NLP Research Group for their feedback during paper clinics, to Mike Zhang for help improving figures, to Nicholas Walker for feedback on multiple drafts of this paper, and to Shreyas Srinivasa for initial input on cybersecurity research norms. Finally, thank you to the TACL area chair and reviewers, whose constructive feedback played a major role in shaping this manuscript."],"id":"S01-000.00-805260","identifier":[{"id":"105011525416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-940152fa-7666-4d73-ac91-b8c1b36d012a"],"keyword":["Cybersecurity","Ethics","Harm Minimization","LLM Security","LLMSec","NLP","NLP Security","NLPSec","Natural Language Processing","Responsible Disclosure","ai ethics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-BC1CE8785D104FED4A53F2AFC5029496"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2504.06669","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/tacl_a_00762","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/774702601/Lent_etal_NLPSec_InTheWild.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"nvidia","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"NVIDIA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heather","key":"lentpau","last":"Lent","locid":"bf19a6f9-9520-4ceb-8a84-f42142d1a422","name":"Lent, Heather","orcid":"0000-0003-3463-0767","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erick","key":"galinkinpau","last":"Galinkin","name":"Galinkin, Erick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yiyi","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"fac63374-6a8b-43fa-b74c-98b4c34fe64f","name":"Chen, Yiyi","orcid":"0000-0001-9977-8960","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Myrup","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dc8aaf34-ac43-4d00-8771-5cbdb8096039","name":"Pedersen, Jens Myrup","orcid":"0000-0002-1903-2921","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","name":"Derczynski, Leon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2504.06669","issn":["2307387X"],"journal":"Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics","pages":"709-743","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics","title_org":"Transactions of the Association for Computational Linguistics (TACL)","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105011525416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-940152fa-7666-4d73-ac91-b8c1b36d012a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"NLP Security and Ethics, in the Wild","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805260","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Few-shot classification is a powerful technique, but training requires substantial computing power and data. We propose an efficient method with small model sizes and less training data with only 2-8 training instances per class. Our proposed method, AncSetFit, targets low data scenarios by anchoring the task and label information through sentence embeddings in fine-tuning a Sentence Transformer model. It uses contrastive learning and a triplet loss to enforce training instances of a class to be closest to its own textual semantic label information in the embedding space-and thereby learning to embed different class instances more distinct. AncSetFit obtains strong performance in data-sparse scenarios compared to existing methods across SST-5, Emotion detection, and AG News data, even with just two examples per class.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","Derczynski, Leon","Assent, Ira"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-708696"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anchoring fine tuning of sentence transformer with semantic label information for efficient truly few shot classification","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.emnlp-main.692","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-708696","identifier":[{"id":"85184823454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9d038070-0521-4103-b651-9af842a983d5"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9689D9E642007276884579E1A7245505"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.emnlp-main.692","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalie Brogaard","key":"paulipau","last":"Pauli","locid":"6619aaa8-f1c0-4a8a-8d04-23bcf5b0c7ba","name":"Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","name":"Derczynski, Leon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ira","key":"assentpau","last":"Assent","locid":"012c1c28-bfa9-4107-bd8f-97dae008b06d","name":"Assent, Ira","orcid":"0000-0002-1091-9948","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Houda","key":"bouamorpedh","last":"Bouamor","name":"Bouamor, Houda","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan","key":"pinopedh","last":"Pino","name":"Pino, Juan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kalika","key":"balipedh","last":"Bali","name":"Bali, Kalika","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.emnlp-main.692","pages":"11254-11264","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2023 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184823454"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9d038070-0521-4103-b651-9af842a983d5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Anchoring Fine-tuning of Sentence Transformer with Semantic Label Information for Efficient Truly Few-shot Classification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-708696","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes our submission to the SemEval 2023 Task 3 on two subtasks: detecting persuasion techniques and framing. Both subtasks are multi-label classification problems. We present a set of experiments, exploring how to get robust performance across languages using pre-trained RoBERTa models. We test different oversampling strategies, a strategy of adding textual features from predictions obtained with related models, and present both inconclusive and negative results. We achieve a robust ranking across languages and subtasks with our best ranking being nr. 1 for Subtask 3 on Spanish.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","Pablos Sarabia, Rafael","Derczynski, Leon","Assent, Ira"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-709374"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"teamampa at semeval 000000002023 task 000000000003 exploring multilabel and multilingual roberta models for persuasion and framing detection","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.semeval-1.117","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-709374","identifier":[{"id":"85175398805","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d410b31b-3b54-4f44-baa3-78873b9994fa"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D75CA288EF5908D573ECF0F3133151DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2023.semeval-1.117","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalie Brogaard","key":"paulipau","last":"Pauli","locid":"6619aaa8-f1c0-4a8a-8d04-23bcf5b0c7ba","name":"Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rafael","key":"pablossarabiapau","last":"Pablos Sarabia","locid":"18dcd220-cd90-4982-8b45-6adca44b3911","name":"Pablos Sarabia, Rafael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","name":"Derczynski, Leon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ira","key":"assentpau","last":"Assent","locid":"012c1c28-bfa9-4107-bd8f-97dae008b06d","name":"Assent, Ira","orcid":"0000-0002-1091-9948","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Atul Kr.","key":"ojhapedh","last":"Ojha","name":"Ojha, Atul Kr.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"A. Seza","key":"doğruözpedh","last":"Doğruöz","name":"Doğruöz, A. Seza","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Giovanni","key":"dasanmartinopedh","last":"Da San Martino","name":"Da San Martino, Giovanni","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Harish","key":"tayyarmadabushipedh","last":"Tayyar Madabushi","name":"Tayyar Madabushi, Harish","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ritesh","key":"kumarpedh","last":"Kumar","name":"Kumar, Ritesh","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Elisa","key":"sartoripedh","last":"Sartori","name":"Sartori, Elisa","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.semeval-1.117","pages":"847-855","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 17th International Workshop on Semantic Evaluation (SemEval-2023)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175398805"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d410b31b-3b54-4f44-baa3-78873b9994fa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"TeamAmpa at SemEval-2023 Task 3 : Exploring Multilabel and Multilingual RoBERTa Models for Persuasion and Framing Detection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-709374","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Misinformation has become a major concern in recent last years given its spread across our information sources. In the past years, many NLP tasks have been introduced in this area, with some systems reaching good results on English language datasets. Existing AI based approaches for fighting misinformation in literature suggest automatic stance detection as an integral first step to success. Our paper aims at utilizing this progress made for English to transfers that knowledge into other languages, which is a non-trivial task due to the domain gap between English and the target languages. We propose a black-box non-intrusive method that utilizes techniques from Domain Adaptation to reduce the domain gap, without requiring any human expertise in the target language, by leveraging low-quality data in both a supervised and unsupervised manner. This allows us to rapidly achieve similar results for stance detection.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Dlamini, Gcinizwe","BEKKOUCH, Imad Eddine Ibrahim","Khan, Adil","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382488"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Russia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Innopolis University","Sorbonne University"],"keyword":["Disinformation","Domain adaptation","Less resourced languages","Misinformation","Stance Detection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging the domain gap for stance detection for the zulu language","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90392596/zulu_stance_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-