{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Kirk, Hannah Rose","Birhane, Abeba","Vidgen, Bertie","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381482"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mozilla Foundation","The Alan Turing Institute","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"handling and presenting harmful text in nlp research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90392679/handling_and_presenting_harmful_text_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381482","ids":["itu-0ea18c38-9577-474f-a231-7b7760b95960"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A82AA8810DA3A582394DA9CD531D5A32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90392679/handling_and_presenting_harmful_text_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"mozilla foundation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Mozilla Foundation","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"the alan turing institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Alan Turing Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hannah Rose","key":"kirkpau","last":"Kirk","name":"Kirk, Hannah Rose","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Abeba","key":"birhanepau","last":"Birhane","name":"Birhane, Abeba","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bertie","key":"vidgenpau","last":"Vidgen","name":"Vidgen, Bertie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Findings of EMNLP"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0ea18c38-9577-474f-a231-7b7760b95960"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Handling and Presenting Harmful Text in NLP Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381482","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"It is important to understand how people use words to persuade each other. This helps understand debate, and detect persuasive narratives in regard to e.g. misinformation. While computational modelling of some aspects of persuasion has received some attention, a way to unify and describe the overall phenomenon of when persuasion becomes undesired and problematic, is missing. In this paper, we attempt to address this by proposing a taxonomy of computational persuasion. Drawing upon existing research and resources, this paper shows how to re-frame and re-organise current work into a coherent framework targeting the misuse of rhetorical appeals. As a study to validate these re-framings, we then train and evaluate models of persuasion adapted to our taxonomy. Our results show an application of our taxonomy, and we are able to detecting misuse of rhetorical appeals, finding that these are more often used in misinformative contexts than in true ones.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","Derczynski, Leon","Assent, Ira"],"cuid":["S02-082.20-014653"],"event":{"end":"2022-12-07","place":"Abu Dhabi","start":"2022-12-07","title":"Workshop on NLP for Positive Impact 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling persuasion through misuse of rhetorical appeals","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2022.nlp4pi-1.11","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.20-014653","identifier":[{"id":"85151331877","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1c3d2588-0340-4366-ae5f-837e553dc260","itu-36d2b5e2-76f4-4c58-b3aa-70491d2b2a14"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C4D7B2A6DE94D1194D366EC69F2DE99"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/90392646/wokrshop_social_impact.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90392646/wokrshop_social_impact.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2022.nlp4pi-1.11","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2022.nlp4pi-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalie Brogaard","key":"paulipau","last":"Pauli","locid":"6619aaa8-f1c0-4a8a-8d04-23bcf5b0c7ba","name":"Pauli, Amalie Brogaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ira","key":"assentpau","last":"Assent","locid":"012c1c28-bfa9-4107-bd8f-97dae008b06d","name":"Assent, Ira","orcid":"0000-0002-1091-9948","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2022.nlp4pi-1.11","eisbn":["9781959429197"],"isbn":["9781959429197"],"pages":"89-100","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"NLP4PI 2022 - 2nd Workshop on NLP for Positive Impact, Proceedings of the Workshop"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151331877"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1c3d2588-0340-4366-ae5f-837e553dc260","itu-36d2b5e2-76f4-4c58-b3aa-70491d2b2a14"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modelling Persuasion through Misuse of Rhetorical Appeals","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.20-014653","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The task of learning to map an input set onto a permuted sequence of its elements is challenging for neural networks. Set-to-sequence problems occur in natural language processing, computer vision and structure prediction, where interactions between elements of large sets define the optimal output. Models must exhibit relational reasoning, handle varying cardinalities and manage combinatorial complexity. Previous attention-based methods require n layers of their set transformations to explicitly represent n-th order relations. Our aim is to enhance their ability to efficiently model higher-order interactions through an additional interdependence component. We propose a novel neural set encoding method called the Set Interdependence Transformer, capable of relating the set's permutation invariant representation to its elements within sets of any cardinality. We combine it with a permutation learning module into a complete, 3-part set-to-sequence model and demonstrate its state-of-the-art performance on a number of tasks. These range from combinatorial optimization problems, through permutation learning challenges on both synthetic and established NLP datasets for sentence ordering, to a novel domain of product catalog structure prediction. Additionally, the network's ability to generalize to unseen sequence lengths is investigated and a comparative empirical analysis of the existing methods' ability to learn higher-order interactions is provided.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jurewicz, Mateusz","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383677"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Higher order interactions","Permutation learning","Relational reasoning","Set Interdependence Transformer","Set to sequence problems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"set interdependence transformer set to sequence neural networks for permutation learning and structure prediction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90392566/IJCAI_2022_Set_to_Sequence.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383677","ids":["itu-a52390d8-f039-4666-9641-9d5c6ddb4eb7"],"keyword":["Higher-order interactions","Permutation learning","Relational reasoning","Set Interdependence Transformer","Set-to-sequence problems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4DC8BC331347CCBA4B411A2BF5CBBC30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90392566/IJCAI_2022_Set_to_Sequence.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mateusz","key":"jurewiczpau","last":"Jurewicz","name":"Jurewicz, Mateusz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings on the International Joint Conferences on Artificial Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a52390d8-f039-4666-9641-9d5c6ddb4eb7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Set Interdependence Transformer: Set-to-Sequence Neural Networks for Permutation Learning and Structure Prediction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383677","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In our role as program committee co-chairs for COLING 2018, we tried out several innovations in the process of creating the conference program, with the following goals: (1) creating a program of high quality papers which represent diverse approaches to and applications of computational linguistics written and presented by researchers from throughout our international community; (2) facilitating thoughtful reviewing which is both informative to area chairs (and PC co-chairs) and helpful to authors; and (3) ensuring that the results published at COLING 2018 are as reproducible as possible. This short paper outlines the innovations and reflects on the ways in which they helped (or didn’t) to achieve those goals.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon","Bender, Emily M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789567"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Computational linguistics","Peer review","Reproducibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards better interdisciplinary science learnings from coling 000000002018","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108200849/CL_learnings_from_COLING_pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789567","ids":["itu-ac4b1bc7-a730-4ca6-9664-2cf4d31f6aaf"],"keyword":["Computational linguistics","Conference program management","Diversity of approaches","Peer review","Reproducibility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A6FDECC071F4D447481FA3A7C3DFF440"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108200849/CL_learnings_from_COLING_pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emily M.","key":"benderpau","last":"Bender","name":"Bender, Emily M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2021-208","pages":"21","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2021-208","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ac4b1bc7-a730-4ca6-9664-2cf4d31f6aaf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards better interdisciplinary science: Learnings from COLING 2018","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789567","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Online misogyny, a category of online abusive language, has serious and harmful social consequences. Automatic detection of misogynistic language online, while imperative, poses complicated challenges to both data gathering, data annotation, and bias mitigation, as this type of data is linguistically complex and diverse. This paper makes three contributions in this area: Firstly, we describe the detailed design of our iterative annotation process and codebook. Secondly, we present a comprehensive taxonomy of labels for annotating misogyny in natural written language, and finally, we introduce a high-quality dataset of annotated posts sampled from social media posts.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zeinert, Philine","Inie, Nanna","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381861"],"event":{"acronym":"IJCNPL","title":"International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automatic detection","Bias Mitigation","Data Annotation","Online Misogyny","Social media analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"annotating online misogyny","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86115829/annotating_online_misogyny_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381861","ids":["itu-274d2228-a805-4763-994d-7c2951a0c8a1"],"keyword":["Automatic Detection","Bias Mitigation","Data Annotation","Online Misogyny","Social Media Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6127DA6DD479E6BA729E0DE338CDF07A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.