{"abstract":"Automatic language identification is a challenging problem. Discriminating between closely related languages is especially difficult. This paper presents a machine learning approach for automatic language identification for the Nordic languages, which often suffer miscategorisation by existing state-of-the-art tools. Concretely we will focus on discrimination between six Nordic languages: Danish, Swedish, Norwegian (Nynorsk), Norwegian (Bokmål), Faroese and Icelandic.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Haas, René","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383564"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automatic language identification","Language discrimination","Machine learning","Natal differentiation","Nordic languages"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discriminating between similar nordic languages","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2021.vardial-1.8/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383564","ids":["itu-9d31bf14-54be-41ad-88a7-9396a2d681a5"],"keyword":["Automatic language identification","Language discrimination","Machine learning","Natal differentiation","Nordic languages"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1713DA9C31AFA722C22E40BE96FBB143"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2021.vardial-1.8/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85902115/NordicDSL_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"haaspau","last":"Haas","name":"Haas, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"67-75","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Eighth Workshop on NLP for Similar Languages, Varieties and Dialects"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9d31bf14-54be-41ad-88a7-9396a2d681a5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discriminating Between Similar Nordic Languages","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383564","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Machine learning on sets towards sequential output is an important and ubiquitous task, with applications ranging from language modelling and meta-learning to multi-agent strategy games and power grid optimization. Combining elements of representation learning and structured prediction, its two primary challenges include obtaining a meaningful, permutation invariant set representation and subsequently utilizing this representation to output a complex target permutation. This paper provides a comprehensive introduction to the field as well as an overview of important machine learning methods tackling both of these key challenges, with a detailed qualitative comparison of selected model architectures.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jurewicz, Mateusz","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384092"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Machine learning","Neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"set to sequence methods in machine learning a review","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1613/jair.1.12839","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384092","identifier":[{"id":"85114116208","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c1763688-224e-4c3d-919a-1261bc739192"],"keyword":["machine learning","neural networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-37F8F15AC41BDD9FA6DDDCCD84FBC2C2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86138636/Set_to_Sequence_Methods_in_Machine_Learning_a_Review.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1613/jair.1.12839","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://jair.org/index.php/jair/article/view/12839/26707","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mateusz","key":"jurewiczpau","last":"Jurewicz","name":"Jurewicz, Mateusz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1613/jair.1.12839","issn":["10769757","19435037"],"issn_org":["10769757"],"journal":"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research","pages":"885-924","publisher":"AAAI Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research","title_org":"The Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114116208"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1763688-224e-4c3d-919a-1261bc739192"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Set-to-Sequence Methods in Machine Learning: A Review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384092","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Detecting and grounding false and misleading claims on the web has grown to form a substantial sub-field of NLP. The sub-field addresses problems at multiple different levels of misinformation detection: identifying check-worthy claims; tracking claims and rumors; rumor collection and annotation; grounding claims against knowledge bases; using stance to verify claims; and applying style analysis to detect deception. This half-day tutorial presents the theory behind each of these steps as well as the state-of-the-art solutions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon","Zubiaga, Arkaitz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384071"],"event":{"acronym":"COLING","title":"International Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Claim Verification","Deceptive Language Detection","Misinformation Detection","Natural Language Processing","Rumor Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"detection and resolution of rumors and misinformation with nlp","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.coling-tutorials.4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384071","identifier":[{"id":"85129834343","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bfbf7f68-f45d-4875-8e1e-99e6f8584aca"],"keyword":["Claim Verification","Deceptive Language Detection","Misinformation Detection","Natural Language Processing","Rumor Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-628759027C8E33943B7E590D454F6ACD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.coling-tutorials.4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.coling-tutorials.4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85669563/2020.coling_tutorials.4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Arkaitz","key":"zubiagapau","last":"Zubiaga","name":"Zubiaga, Arkaitz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.coling-tutorials.4","eisbn":["9781952148309"],"pages":"22-26","place":"Barcelona, Spain (Online)","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 28th International Conference on Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129834343"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bfbf7f68-f45d-4875-8e1e-99e6f8584aca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Detection and Resolution of Rumors and Misinformation with NLP","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384071","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We aimed to investigate whether daily fluctuations in mental health-relevant Twitter posts are associated with daily fluctuations in mental health crisis episodes. We conducted a primary and replicated time-series analysis of retrospectively collected data from Twitter and two London mental healthcare providers. Daily numbers of ‘crisis episodes’ were defined as incident inpatient, home treatment team and crisis house referrals between 2010 and 2014. Higher volumes of depression and schizophrenia tweets were associated with higher numbers of same-day crisis episodes for both sites. After adjusting for temporal trends, seven-day lagged analyses showed significant positive associations on day 1, changing to negative associations by day 4 and reverting to positive associations by day 7. There was a 15% increase in crisis episodes on days with above-median schizophrenia-related Twitter posts. A temporal association was thus found between Twitter-wide mental health-related social media content and crisis episodes in mental healthcare replicated across two services. Seven-day associations are consistent with both precipitating and longer-term risk associations. Sizes of effects were large enough to have potential local and national relevance and further research is needed to evaluate how services might better anticipate times of higher risk and identify the most vulnerable groups.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kolliakou, Anna","Bakolis, Ioannis","Chandran, David","Derczynski, Leon","Werbeloff, Nomi","Osborn, David PJ","Bontcheva, Kalina","Rob, Stewart"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384565"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King’s College London","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Human behaviour"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mental health related conversations on social media and crisis episodes a time series regression analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-57835-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384565","identifier":[{"id":"85079059473","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e0379795-4d3e-487f-a300-a2e5ea3edb7d"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Human behaviour"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C8897F1CE775C1D14124C66123B8A32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84858214/Stigma_paper.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-57835-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King’s College London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"kolliakoupau","last":"Kolliakou","name":"Kolliakou, Anna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ioannis","key":"bakolispau","last":"Bakolis","name":"Bakolis, Ioannis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"chandranpau","last":"Chandran","name":"Chandran, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nomi","key":"werbeloffpau","last":"Werbeloff","name":"Werbeloff, Nomi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David PJ","key":"osbornpau","last":"Osborn","name":"Osborn, David PJ","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kalina","key":"bontchevapau","last":"Bontcheva","name":"Bontcheva, Kalina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stewart","key":"robpau","last":"Rob","name":"Rob, Stewart","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-57835-9","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"1342","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079059473"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e0379795-4d3e-487f-a300-a2e5ea3edb7d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mental health-related conversations on social media and crisis episodes: a time-series regression analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384565","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The presence of offensive language on social media platforms and the implications this poses is becoming a major concern in modern society. Given the enormous amount of content created every day, automatic methods are required to detect and deal with this type of content. Until now, most of the research has focused on solving the problem for the English language, while the problem is multilingual. We construct a Danish dataset DKHATE containing user-generated comments from various social media platforms, and to our knowledge, the first of its kind, annotated for various types and target of offensive language. We develop four automatic classification systems, each designed to work for both the English and the Danish language. In the detection of offensive language in English, the best performing system achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0:74, and the best performing system for Danish achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0:70. In the detection of whether or not an offensive post is targeted, the best performing system for English achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0:62, while the best performing system for Danish achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0:73. Finally, in the detection of the target type in a targeted offensive post, the best performing system for English achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0:56, and the best performing system for Danish achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0:63. Our work for both the English and the Danish language captures the type and targets of offensive language, and present automatic methods for detecting different kinds of offensive language such as hate speech and cyberbullying.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sigurbergsson, Guðbjartur","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384008"],"event":{"acronym":"LREC","title":"International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automatic classification","Hate speech detection","Multilingual dataset","Offensive language detection","Social media platforms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"offensive language and hate speech detection for danish","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85287367/2020.lrec_1.430.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384008","identifier":[{"id":"85092256646","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bb9b25ce-3bbf-4418-b3e3-1c086d105ff0"],"keyword":["Automatic classification","Hate speech detection","Multilingual dataset","Offensive language detection","Social media platforms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2D3982E1B4B4351076D1B3B888716DFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85287367/2020.lrec_1.430.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.derczynski.com/papers/danish_hsd.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Guðbjartur","key":"sigurbergssonpau","last":"Sigurbergsson","name":"Sigurbergsson, Guðbjartur","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9791095546344"],"pages":"3498-3508","publisher":"European Language Resources Association","status":"p","subtitle":"LREC 2020","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092256646"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bb9b25ce-3bbf-4418-b3e3-1c086d105ff0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Offensive Language and Hate Speech Detection for Danish","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384008","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Danish is a North Germanic/Scandinavian language spoken primarily in Denmark, a country with a tradition of technological and scientific innovation. However, from a technological perspective, the Danish language has received relatively little attention and, as a result, Danish language technology is hard to develop, in part due to a lack of large or broad-coverage Danish corpora. This paper describes the Danish Gigaword project, which aims to construct a freely-available one billion word corpus of Danish text that represents the breadth of the written language.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Strømberg-Derczynski, Leon","Baglini, Rebekah Brita","Christiansen, Morten H.","Ciosici, Manuel R.","Dalsgaard, Jacob Aarup","Fusaroli, Riccardo","Henrichsen, Peter Juel","Hvingelby, Rasmus Stig","Kirkedal, Andreas","Kjeldsen, Alex Speed","Ladefoged, Claus","Nielsen, Finn Årup","Petersen, Malte Lau","Rystrøm, Jonathan Hvithamar","Varab, Daniel"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-022287"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Weill Cornell Medical College"],"keyword":["cs CL"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish gigaword project","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2005.03521.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-022287","ids":["au-83d64365-b705-4023-8d50-944585