{"abstract":"We propose two measures for measuring the quality of constructed claims in the FEVER task. Annotating data for this task involves the creation of supporting and refuting claims over a set of evidence. Automatic annotation processes often leave superficial patterns in data, which learning systems can detect instead of performing the underlying task. Humans also can leave these superficial patterns, either voluntarily or involuntarily (due to e.g. fatigue). The two measures introduced attempt to detect the impact of these superficial patterns. One is a new information-theoretic and distributionality based measure, DCI; and the other an extension of neural probing work over the ARCT task, utility. We demonstrate these measures over a recent major dataset, that from the English FEVER task in 2019.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schulte, Henri","Binau, Julie","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381822"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Claim Quality Metrics","Data Annotation","FEVER Task","Information Theoretic Measure","Superficial Patterns"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"maintaining quality in fever annotation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85287456/2020.fever_1.6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381822","identifier":[{"id":"85115001066","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-24f3e985-9622-405a-b47d-b4ee4e341717"],"keyword":["Claim Quality Metrics","Data Annotation","FEVER Task","Information-Theoretic Measure","Superficial Patterns"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8DE9F65018425C43B6C9D95B20941E0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85287456/2020.fever_1.6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Henri","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, Henri","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie","key":"binaupau","last":"Binau","name":"Binau, Julie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781952148101"],"pages":"42-46","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","subtitle":"Association for Computational Linguistics","title":"Proceedings of the Third Workshop on Fact Extraction and VERification (FEVER)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115001066"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-24f3e985-9622-405a-b47d-b4ee4e341717"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Maintaining quality in FEVER annotation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381822","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Spread of misinformation presents a technological and so- cial threat to society. With the advance of AI-based lan- guage models, automatically generated texts have be- come difficult to identify and easy to create at scale. We present the “Rumour Mill\", a playful art piece, designed as a commentary on the spread of rumours and automatically- generated misinformation. The mill is a tabletop interactive machine, which invites a user to experience the process of creating believable text by interacting with different tangible controls on the mill. The user manipulates visible parame- ters to adjust the genre and type of an automatically gener- ated text rumour. The Rumour Mill is a physical demonstra- tion of the state of NLP technology and its ability to gener- ate and manipulate natural language text, and of the act of starting and spreading rumours.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Falk Olesen, Jeanette","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382325"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["AI based language models","Misinformation","Natural Language Processing NLP","automated text generation","interactive machine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the rumour mill making the spread of misinformation explicit and tangible","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84873742/Rumour_Mill_CHI2020_extended_abstract.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382325","identifier":[{"id":"85090187632","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-472705ce-0e79-4f50-898f-847771c1d6ca"],"keyword":["AI-based language models","automated text generation","interactive machine","misinformation","natural language processing (NLP)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-A0A2E3124158E55649E91066BC11B5F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84873742/Rumour_Mill_CHI2020_extended_abstract.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"falkolesenpau","last":"Falk Olesen","name":"Falk Olesen, Jeanette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3334480.3383159","eisbn":["9781450368193/20/04"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"The ACM CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090187632"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-472705ce-0e79-4f50-898f-847771c1d6ca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Rumour Mill: Making the Spread of Misinformation Explicit and Tangible","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382325","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Word clustering groups words that exhibit similar properties. One popular method for this is Brown clustering, which uses short-range distributional information to construct clusters. Specifically, this is a hard hierarchical clustering with a fixed-width beam that employs bi-grams and greedily minimizes global mutual information loss. The result is word clusters that tend to outperform or complement other word representations, especially when constrained by small datasets. However, Brown clustering has high computational complexity and does not lend itself to parallel computation. This, together with the lack of efficient implementations, limits their applicability in NLP. We present efficient implementations of Brown clustering and the alternative Exchange clustering as well as a number of methods to accelerate the computation of both hierarchical and flat clusters. We show empirically that clusters obtained with the accelerated method match the performance of clusters computed using the original methods.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ciosici, Manuel Rafael","Assent, Ira","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S02-094.05-020250"],"event":{"acronym":"LREC","end":"2020-05-16","place":"Marseille, fr","start":"2020-05-11","title":"International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Brown clustering","Computational complexity","Efficient computation","Hierarchical clustering","Mutual information","Word clustering","Word representations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accelerated high quality mutual information based word clustering","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.lrec-1.303.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.05-020250","identifier":[{"id":"85096595225","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-683c30bc-4ec6-496b-b4d3-c3b9dc231204","itu-18899d4b-bb76-4fa9-be4f-25976e24ebce"],"keyword":["Brown clustering","Computational complexity","Efficient computation","Hierarchical clustering","Mutual information","Word clustering","Word clusters","Word representations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-78070B9BA1031EE847ED738E8530874D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85287515/2020.lrec_1.303.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.lrec-1.303/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.lrec-1.303.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Manuel R.","key":"ciosicipau","last":"Ciosici","locid":"8e303d7a-7edf-4fce-8527-a44449a0a702","name":"Ciosici, Manuel Rafael","name_org":"Ciosici, Manuel R.","orcid":"0000-0001-7768-738X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ira","key":"assentpau","last":"Assent","locid":"012c1c28-bfa9-4107-bd8f-97dae008b06d","name":"Assent, Ira","orcid":"0000-0002-1091-9948","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9791095546344"],"isbn":["9791095546344"],"pages":"2491-2496","place":"Marseille","publisher":"European Language Resources Association","status":"p","title":"LREC 2020 - 12th International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation, Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096595225"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-683c30bc-4ec6-496b-b4d3-c3b9dc231204","itu-18899d4b-bb76-4fa9-be4f-25976e24ebce"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Accelerated High-Quality Mutual-Information Based Word Clustering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.05-020250","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Misinformation spread presents a technological and social threat to society. With the advance of AI-based language models, automatically generated texts have become difficult to identify and easy to create at scale. We present \"The Rumour Mill\", a playful art piece, designed as a commentary on the spread of rumours and automatically-generated misinformation. The mill is a tabletop interactive machine, which invites a user to experience the process of creating believable text by interacting with different tangible controls on the mill. The user manipulates visible parameters to adjust the genre and type of an automatically generated text rumour. The Rumour Mill is a physical demonstration of the state of current technology and its ability to generate and manipulate natural language text, and of the act of starting and spreading rumours.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Falk Olesen, Jeanette","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-242499"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2020-04-30","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2020-04-25","title":"CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs CL","cs HC"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the rumour mill making the spread of misinformation explicit and tangible","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090187632","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-242499","identifier":[{"id":"85090187632","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c637936c-269a-4e9e-b6d6-209cab59ccc1"],"keyword":["cs.CL","cs.HC"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-A0A2E3124158E55649E91066BC11B5F5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Digital Design and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette Falk","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"8d0554b5-436a-4db6-85e2-eb0ad4cf341f","name":"Falk Olesen, Jeanette","name_org":"Olesen, Jeanette Falk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","name":"Derczynski, Leon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3334480.3383159","eisbn":["9781450368193"],"isbn":["9781450368193"],"place":"USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI EA 2020 - Extended Abstracts of the 2020 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090187632"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c637936c-269a-4e9e-b6d6-209cab59ccc1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Rumour Mill : Making the Spread of Misinformation Explicit and Tangible","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-242499","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Data-driven and machine learning based approaches for detecting, categorising and measuring abusive content such as hate speech and harassment have gained traction due to their scalability, robustness and increasingly high performance. Making effective detection systems for abusive content relies on having the right training datasets, reflecting a widely accepted mantra in computer science: Garbage In, Garbage Out. However, creating training datasets which are large, varied, theoretically-informed and that minimize biases is difficult, laborious and requires deep expertise. This paper systematically reviews 63 publicly available training datasets which have been created to train abusive language classifiers. It also reports on creation of a dedicated website for cataloguing abusive language data hatespeechdata.com. We discuss the challenges and opportunities of open science in this field, and argue that although more dataset sharing would bring many benefits it also poses social and ethical risks which need careful consideration. Finally, we provide evidence-based recommendations for practitioners creating new abusive content training datasets.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Vidgen, Bertie","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383202"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The Alan Turing Institute"],"keyword":["Internet","Language","Machine learning","Metadata","Social discrimination","Speech","Taxonomy","Twitter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"directions in abusive language training data a systematic review garbage in garbage out","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0243300","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383202","identifier":[{"id":"85098917139","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-838f076b-bf31-4f59-9744-bae123f0a785"],"keyword":["Internet","Language","Metadata","Social discrimination","Speech","Twitter","machine learning","taxonomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2341FEA46FF75D7E32AA8A7BF7771CB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0243300","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85658040/Directions_in_abusive_language_training_data.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"the alan turing institute","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Alan Turing Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bertie","key":"vidgenpau","last":"Vidgen","name":"Vidgen, Bertie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0243300","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"12","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0243300","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098917139"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-838f076b-bf31-4f59-9744-bae123f0a785"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Directions in abusive language training data, a systematic review: Garbage in, garbage out","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383202","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We present the results and main findings of SemEval-2020 Task 12 on Multilingual Offensive Language Identification in Social Media (OffensEval 2020). The task involves three subtasks corresponding to the hierarchical taxonomy of the OLID schema (Zampieri et al., 2019a) from OffensEval 2019. The task featured five languages: English, Arabic, Danish, Greek, and Turkish for Subtask A. In addition, English also featured Subtasks B and C. OffensEval 2020 was one of the most popular tasks at SemEval-2020 attracting a large number of participants across all subtasks and also across all languages. A total of 528 teams signed up to participate in the task, 145 teams submitted systems during the evaluation period, and 70 submitted system description papers.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Zampieri, Marcos","Nakov, Preslav","Rosenthal, Sara","Atanasova, Pepa","Karadzhov, Georgi","Mubarak, Hamdy","Derczynski, Leon","Pitenis, Zeses","Coltekin, Cagri"],"cuid":["S02-087.49-768533"],"event":{"acronym":"SemEval","title":"International Workshop on Semantic Evaluation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Qatar","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eberhard Karls University of Tübingen","IBM","IBM Research","Qatar Computing Research institute","Rochester Institute of Technology","University of Cambridge","University of Tübingen","University of Wolverhampton"],"keyword":["Hierarchical Taxonomy","Multilingual Offensive Language Identification","OffensEval 2020","SemEval 2020","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"semeval 000000002020 task 000000000012 multilingual offensive language identification in social media offenseval 000000002020","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.semeval-1.188","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.49-768533","identifier":[{"id":"85123932428","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2619c87f-b285-413f-b331-c8594f3a4c32","ku-6cf4b4ce-0baf-4887-8fd3-6c383434ccb1"],"keyword":["Hierarchical Taxonomy","Multilingual Offensive Language Identification","OffensEval 2020","SemEval-2020","Social Media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1DA515A9E2FCA6D5489B7E232ACBF225"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/2020.semeval-1.188.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.semeval-1.188","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411941910/SemEval_2020_Task_12.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85674714/2020.semeval_1.188.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"rochester institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rochester Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"qa","key":"qatar computing research institute","loc":["Qatar","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Qatar Computing Research institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"ibm research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"IBM Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"ibm","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"IBM","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Univers