{"abstract":"The task of stance detection consists of classifying the opinion within a text towards some target. This paper seeks to generate a dataset of quotes from Danish politicians, label this dataset to allow the task of stance detection to be performed, and present annotation guidelines to allow further expansion of the generated dataset. Furthermore, three models based on an LSTM architecture are designed, implemented and optimized to perform the task of stance detection for the generated dataset. Experiments are performed using conditionality and bi-directionality for these models, and using either singular word embeddings or averaged word embeddings for an entire quote, to determine the optimal model design. The simplest model design, applying neither conditionality or bi-directionality, and averaged word embeddings across quotes, yields the strongest results. Furthermore, it was found that inclusion of the quotes politician, and the party affiliation of the quoted politician, greatly improved performance of the strongest model.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lehmann, Rasmus","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382509"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Annotation Guidelines","Bi directionality","Conditionality","Danish Politicians","Dataset Generation","LSTM Models","Model Optimization","Political Quotes","Stance Detection","Word Embeddings"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"political stance in danish","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84550982/W19_6121.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382509","ids":["itu-52cf5fd6-d57e-499b-bca6-85defa700e30"],"keyword":["Annotation Guidelines","Bi-directionality","Conditionality","Danish Politicians","Dataset Generation","LSTM Models","Model Optimization","Political Quotes","Stance Detection","Word Embeddings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-059FFCD4BA321FCF358B7B8FD40FF10E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/W19-6121.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84550982/W19_6121.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"lehmannpau","last":"Lehmann","name":"Lehmann, Rasmus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789179299958"],"issn":["17366305"],"pages":"197-207","publisher":"Linköping University Press","series":"NEALT (Northern European Association of Language Technology) Proceedings Series","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Nordic Conference of Computational Linguistics (2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-52cf5fd6-d57e-499b-bca6-85defa700e30"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Political Stance in Danish","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382509","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Information extraction systems and techniques have been largely used to deal with the increasing amount of unstructured data available nowadays. Time is among the different kinds of information that may be extracted from such unstructured data sources, including text documents. However, the inability to correctly identify and extract temporal information from text makes it difficult to understand how the extracted events are organised in a chronological order. Furthermore, in many situations, the meaning of temporal expressions (timexes) is imprecise, such as in “less than 2 years” and “several weeks”, and cannot be accurately normalised, leading to interpretation errors. Although there are some approaches that enable representing imprecise timexes, they are not designed to be applied to specific scenarios and difficult to generalise. This paper presents a novel methodology to analyse and normalise imprecise temporal expressions by representing temporal imprecision in the form of membership functions, based on human interpretation of time in two different languages (Portuguese and English). Each resulting model is a generalisation of probability distributions in the form of trapezoidal and hexagonal fuzzy membership functions. We use an adapted F1-score to guide the choice of the best models for each kind of imprecise timex and a weighted F1-score (F13D) as a complementary metric in order to identify relevant differences when comparing two normalisation models. We apply the proposed methodology for three distinct classes of imprecise timexes, and the resulting models give distinct insights in the way each kind of temporal expression is interpreted.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tissot, Hegler","Roberts, Angus","Derczynski, Leon","Didonet Del Fabro, Marcos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383944"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Federal University of Paraná","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Imprecise Timex Normalisation","Information extraction","Natural Language Processing NLP","Temporal Expression Timex"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"normalisation of imprecise temporal expressions extracted from text","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10115-019-01338-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383944","identifier":[{"id":"85061660895","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b78c605c-2424-4256-a64c-f0deb4830908"],"keyword":["Imprecise Timex Normalisation","Information Extraction","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Temporal Expression (Timex)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2528F2BCB85FB7524C44FCAA4F875C7E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84172352/2016_KAIS_ITN_Imprecise_Timex_Normalisation.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10115-019-01338-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"federal university of paraná","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Federal University of Paraná","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hegler","key":"tissotpau","last":"Tissot","name":"Tissot, Hegler","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Angus","key":"robertspau","last":"Roberts","name":"Roberts, Angus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcos","key":"didonetdelfabropau","last":"Didonet Del Fabro","name":"Didonet Del Fabro, Marcos","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10115-019-01338-1","issn":["02191377","02193116"],"issn_org":["02191377"],"journal":"Knowledge and Information Systems","pages":"1-34","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Knowledge and Information Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061660895"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b78c605c-2424-4256-a64c-f0deb4830908"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Normalisation of imprecise temporal expressions extracted from text","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383944","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This technical note describes a set of baseline tools for automatic processing of Danish text. The tools are machine-learning based, using natural language processing models trained over previously annotated documents. They are maintained at ITU Copenhagen and will always be freely available.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384357"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Annotated Corpora","Baseline Tools","Danish Text Processing","Machine learning","Natural Language Processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simple natural language processing tools for danish","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1906.11608.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384357","identifier":[{"id":"85094039243","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d221244a-02c3-46c2-878a-297e1ebb3a14"],"keyword":["Annotated Corpora","Baseline Tools","Danish Text Processing","Machine Learning","Natural Language Processing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A54767A92080D1616E936D4332DBCF60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1906.11608.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d221244a-02c3-46c2-878a-297e1ebb3a14"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Simple Natural Language Processing Tools for Danish","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384357","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Danish is a North Germanic language spoken principally in Denmark, a country with a long tradition of technological and scientific innovation. However, the language has received relatively little attention from a technological perspective. In this paper, we review Natural Language Processing (NLP) research, digital resources and tools which have been developed for Danish. We find that availability of models and tools is limited, which calls for work that lifts Danish NLP a step closer to the privileged languages. Dansk abstrakt: Dansk er et nordgermansk sprog, talt primært i kongeriget Danmark, et land med stærk tradition for teknologisk og videnskabelig innovation. Det danske sprog har imidlertid været genstand for relativt begrænset opmærksomhed, teknologisk set. I denne artikel gennemgår vi sprogteknologi-forskning, -ressourcer og -værktøjer udviklet for dansk. Vi konkluderer at der eksisterer et fåtal af modeller og værktøjer, hvilket indbyder til forskning som løfter dansk sprogteknologi i niveau med mere priviligerede sprog.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kirkedal, Andreas Søeborg","Plank, Barbara","Derczynski, Leon","Schluter, Natalie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384150"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Danish language","Digital resources","Natural Language Processing NLP","Technological innovation","linguistic tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the lacunae of danish natural language processing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84551035/W19_6141.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384150","ids":["itu-c4ada506-a42e-465f-88b3-4007eccdc03e"],"keyword":["Danish language","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","digital resources","linguistic tools","technological innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A4CAA5EB28526A34F399035105BB77BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/W19-6141.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84551035/W19_6141.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Søeborg","key":"kirkedalpau","last":"Kirkedal","name":"Kirkedal, Andreas Søeborg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalie","key":"schluterpau","last":"Schluter","locid":"879e7ac4-e64c-4c5f-9591-421e56cd0678","name":"Schluter, Natalie","orcid":"0000-0001-8215-4801","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789179299958"],"issn":["17366305"],"pages":"356-362","publisher":"Linköping University Press","series":"NEALT (Northern European Association of Language Technology) Proceedings Series","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Nordic Conference of Computational Linguistics (2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c4ada506-a42e-465f-88b3-4007eccdc03e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Lacunae of Danish Natural Language Processing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384150","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces language processing resources and tools for Bornholmsk, a language spoken on the island of Bornholm, with roots in Danish and closely related to Scanian. This presents an overview of the language and available data, and the first NLP models for this living, minority Nordic language. Sammenfattnijng på borrijnholmst: Dæjnna artikkelijn introduserer natursprågsresurser å varktoi for borrijnholmst, ed språg a dær snakkes på ön Borrijnholm me rødder i danst å i nær familia me skånst. Artikkelijn gjer ed âuersyn âuer språged å di datan som fijnnes, å di fosste NLP modællarna for dætta læwenes nordiska minnretâlsspråged.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon","Kjeldsen, Alex Speed"],"cuid":["S02-081.75-038358"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bornholmsk language","Computational models for Bornholmsk","Language resources","Natural Language Processing","Nordic minority languages"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bornholmsk natural language processing resources and tools","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/237148783/W19_6138.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.75-038358","ids":["itu-a5de21af-c653-4895-9b1a-11e3a2e84cb0","ku-fd09e6c7-772e-4c00-8330-aef8ab3c759b"],"keyword":["Bornholmsk language","Computational models for Bornholmsk","Language resources","Natural language processing","Nordic minority languages"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-6BE041CB281CDC76D97C5461304E3786"],"oa_link":[{