ordic Conference of Computational Linguistics (2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a5de21af-c653-4895-9b1a-11e3a2e84cb0","ku-fd09e6c7-772e-4c00-8330-aef8ab3c759b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bornholmsk Natural Language Processing: Resources and Tools","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.75-038358","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The net is rife with rumours that spread through microblogs and social media. Not all the claims in these can be verified. However, recent work has shown that the stances alone that commenters take toward claims can be sufficiently good indicators of claim veracity, using e.g. an HMM that takes conversational stance sequences as the only input. Existing results are monolingual (English) and mono-platform (Twitter). This paper introduces a stance-annotated Reddit dataset for the Danish language, and describes various implementations of stance classification models. Of these, a Linear SVM provides predicts stance best, with 0.76 accuracy / 0.42 macro F1. Stance labels are then used to predict veracity across platforms and also across languages, training on conversations held in one language and using the model on conversations held in another. In our experiments, monolinugal scores reach stance-based veracity accuracy of 0.83 (F1 0.68); applying the model across languages predicts veracity of claims with an accuracy of 0.82 (F1 0.67). This demonstrates the surprising and powerful viability of transferring stance-based veracity prediction across languages.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Edelbo Lillie, Anders","Middelboe, Emil Refsgaard","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382982"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross lingual transfer","Linear SVM","Rumour detection","Social media analysis","Stance classification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"joint rumour stance and veracity prediction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84551085/W19_6122.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382982","ids":["itu-7433b1be-ac3c-4b5e-b4fa-f46e77875ff8"],"keyword":["Cross-lingual transfer","Linear SVM","Rumour detection","Social media analysis","Stance classification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-25603F0B7B0ECBE2FBADE15DC919D759"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84551085/W19_6122.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/W19-6122.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"edelbolilliepau","last":"Edelbo Lillie","name":"Edelbo Lillie, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Refsgaard","key":"middelboepau","last":"Middelboe","name":"Middelboe, Emil Refsgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789179299958"],"issn":["17366305"],"pages":"208-221","publisher":"Linköping University Press","series":"NEALT (Northern European Association of Language Technology) Proceedings Series","status":"p","title":"Nordic Conference of Computational Linguistics (2019)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7433b1be-ac3c-4b5e-b4fa-f46e77875ff8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Joint Rumour Stance and Veracity Prediction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382982","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Brown and Exchange word clusters have long been successfully used as word representations in Natural Language Processing (NLP) systems. Their success has been attributed to their seeming ability to represent both semantic and syntactic information. Using corpora representing several language families, we test the hypothesis that Brown and Exchange word clusters are highly effective at encoding morphosyntactic information. Our experiments show that word clusters are highly capable of distinguishing Parts of Speech. We show that increases in Average Mutual Information, the clustering algorithms' optimization goal, are highly correlated with improvements in encoding of morphosyntactic information. Our results provide empirical evidence that downstream NLP systems addressing tasks dependent on morphosyntactic information can benefit from word cluster features.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ciosici, Manuel Rafael","Derczynski, Leon","Assent, Ira"],"cuid":["S02-081.81-020189"],"event":{"acronym":"NAACL HLT","end":"2019-06-05","place":"Minneapolis, us","start":"2019-06-03","title":"Annual Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Average Mutual Information","Morphosyntactic information","Natural Language Processing","Parts of Speech","Word representations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantifying the morphosyntactic content of brown clusters","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/179022036/N19_1157.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.81-020189","identifier":[{"id":"85085582058","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-674815b3-f2ab-446a-84a1-e55404516f4f","itu-be71de3b-f867-498e-a69b-8c4273f1de1d"],"keyword":["Average Mutual Information","Morphosyntactic information","Natural Language Processing","Parts of Speech","Word representations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F0E0C87787AAA64CC6F87514F6635BB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/179022038/N19_1157.Supplementary.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclweb.org/anthology/papers/N/N19/N19-1157/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84172292/NAACL_Brown_PoS.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/179022036/N19_1157.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Manuel Rafael","key":"ciosicipau","last":"Ciosici","locid":"8e303d7a-7edf-4fce-8527-a44449a0a702","name":"Ciosici, Manuel Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-7768-738X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ira","key":"assentpau","last":"Assent","locid":"012c1c28-bfa9-4107-bd8f-97dae008b06d","name":"Assent, Ira","orcid":"0000-0002-1091-9948","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jill","key":"bursteinpedh","last":"Burstein","name":"Burstein, Jill","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christy","key":"doranpedh","last":"Doran","name":"Doran, Christy","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Thamar","key":"soloriopedh","last":"Solorio","name":"Solorio, Thamar","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781950737130"],"isbn":["9781950737130"],"pages":"1541-1550","place":"Stroudsburg, PA","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","subtitle":"Human Language Technologies","title":"Long and Short Papers","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085582058"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-674815b3-f2ab-446a-84a1-e55404516f4f","itu-be71de3b-f867-498e-a69b-8c4273f1de1d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quantifying the morphosyntactic content of Brown Clusters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.81-020189","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The presence of offensive language on social media platforms and the implications this poses is becoming a major concern in modern society. Given the enormous amount of content created every day, automatic methods are required to detect and deal with this type of content. Until now, most of the research has focused on solving the problem for the English language, while the problem is multilingual. We construct a Danish dataset containing user-generated comments from \\textit{Reddit} and \\textit{Facebook}. It contains user generated comments from various social media platforms, and to our knowledge, it is the first of its kind. Our dataset is annotated to capture various types and target of offensive language. We develop four automatic classification systems, each designed to work for both the English and the Danish language. In the detection of offensive language in English, the best performing system achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0.74, and the best performing system for Danish achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0.70. In the detection of whether or not an offensive post is targeted, the best performing system for English achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0.62, while the best performing system for Danish achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0.73. Finally, in the detection of the target type in a targeted offensive post, the best performing system for English achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0.56, and the best performing system for Danish achieves a macro averaged F1-score of 0.63. Our work for both the English and the Danish language captures the type and targets of offensive language, and present automatic methods for detecting different kinds of offensive language such as hate speech and cyberbullying.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383024"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automatic classification systems","Hate speech detection","Multilingual Datasets","Offensive language detection","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"offensive language and hate speech detection for danish","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1908.04531","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383024","identifier":[{"id":"85093306355","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7732568a-3f3e-40ca-9dc1-a5b815d476aa"],"keyword":["Automatic classification systems","Hate speech detection","Multilingual datasets","Offensive language detection","Social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F2F1BCC7B747009D03FA52D6AF5C6E67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1908.04531","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7732568a-3f3e-40ca-9dc1-a5b815d476aa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Offensive Language and Hate Speech Detection for Danish","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383024","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Since the first RumourEval shared task in 2017, interest in automated claim validation has greatly increased, as the danger of ``fake news'' has become a mainstream concern. However automated support for rumour verification remains in its infancy. It is therefore important that a shared task in this area continues to provide a focus for effort, which is likely to increase. Rumour verification is characterised by the need to consider evolving conversations and news updates to reach a verdict on a rumour's veracity. As in RumourEval 2017 we provided a dataset of dubious posts and ensuing conversations in social media, annotated both for stance and veracity. The social media rumours stem from a variety of breaking news stories and the dataset is expanded to include Reddit as well as new Twitter posts. There were two concrete tasks; rumour stance prediction and rumour verification, which we present in detail along with results achieved by participants. We received 22 system submissions (a 70\\% increase from RumourEval 2017) many of which used state-of-the-art methodology to tackle the challenges involved.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Gorrell, Genevieve","Kochkina, Elena","Liakata, Maria","Aker, Ahmet","Zubiaga, Arkaitz","Bontcheva, Kalina","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383299"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London","University of Sheffield","University of Warwick"],"keyword":["Fake news","Social media","automated claim validation","dataset annotation","rumour verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"semeval 000000002019 task 000000000007 rumoureval 000000002019 determining rumour veracity and support for rumours","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/S19-2147","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383299","ids":["itu-8af2d48b-f36b-49b9-9f17-18ee5599a026"],"keyword":["automated claim validation","dataset annotation","fake news","rumour verification","social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B1FF5F33374B2EFFF08554FB0857FB0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/S19-2147","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84235440/Task_paper_SemEval_2019_Task_7_RumourEval_2019_Determining_Rumour_Veracity_and_Support_for_Rumours_1_.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of warwick","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warwick","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Genevieve","key":"gorrellpau","last":"Gorrell","name":"Gorrell, Genevieve","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"kochkinapau","last":"Kochkina","name":"Kochkina, Elena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"liakatapau","last":"Liakata","name":"Liakata, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmet","key":"akerpau","last":"Aker","name":"Aker, Ahmet","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Arkaitz","key":"zubiagapau","last":"Zubiaga","name":"Zubiaga, Arkaitz","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kalina","key":"bontchevapau","last":"Bontcheva","name":"Bontcheva, Kalina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781950737062"],"pages":"845-854","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","subtitle":"NAACL HLT 2019","title":"Proceedings of the 13th International Workshop on Semantic Evaluation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8af2d48b-f36b-49b9-9f17-18ee5599a026"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SemEval-2019 Task 7: RumourEval 2019: Determining Rumour Veracity and Support for Rumours","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383299","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Elections are a time when communication is important in democracies, including over social media. This paper describes a case study of applying NLP to determine the extent to which misinformation and external manipulation were present on Twitter during a national election. We use three methods to detect the spread of misinformation: analysing unusual spatial and temporal behaviours; detecting known false claims and using these to estimate the total prevalence; and detecting amplifiers through language use. We find that while present, detectable spread of misinformation on Twitter was remarkably low during the election period in Denmark.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon","Albert-Lindqvist, Torben Oskar","Bendsen, Marius Venø","Inie, Nanna","Pedersen, Jens Egholm","Pedersen, Viktor Due"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381962"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Elections","Misinformation Detection","NLP","Social media","Twitter Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"misinformation on twitter during the danish national election a case study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84747296/paper_16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381962","ids":["itu-2f158a6e-3156-4a0f-a28c-a55b1556f1d0"],"keyword":["Elections","Misinformation Detection","NLP","Social Media","Twitter Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-59237FBC317F886B5A4414757BB9EDB5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://truthandtrustonline.files.wordpress.com/2019/09/paper_16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84747296/paper_16.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Lix Technologies ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskileonpau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Oskar","key":"albertlindqvisttorbenoskarpau","last":"Albert-Lindqvist","name":"Albert-Lindqvist, Torben Oskar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marius Venø","key":"bendsenmariusvenøpau","last":"Bendsen","name":"Bendsen, Marius Venø","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"inienannapau","last":"Inie","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Egholm","key":"pedersenjensegholmpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Jens Egholm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktor Due","key":"pedersenviktorduepau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Viktor Due","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the conference on Truth and Trust Online"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","lix technologies aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2f158a6e-3156-4a0f-a28c-a55b1556f1d0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Misinformation on Twitter During the Danish National Election: A Case Study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381962","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes the IUCM entry at SemEval-2018 Task 11, on machine comprehension using commonsense knowledge. First, clustering and topic modeling are used to divide given texts into topics. Then, during the answering phase, other texts of the same topic are retrieved and used as commonsense knowledge. Finally, the answer is selected. While clustering itself shows good results, finding an answer proves to be more challenging. This paper reports the results of system evaluation and suggests potential improvements.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Reznikova, Sofia","Derczynski, Leon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382204"],"event":{"acronym":"ACL","title":"Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU"],"country":["Russia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Innopolis University"],"keyword":["Clustering","System evaluation","Topic modeling","commonsense knowledge","machine comprehension"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"iucm at semeval 000000002018 task 000000000011 similar topic texts as a comprehension knowledge source","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/S18-1179","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382204","identifier":[{"id":"85122335796","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3f81dc90-5376-4411-931a-3a6f93bc4a6d"],"keyword":["clustering","commonsense knowledge","machine comprehension","system evaluation","topic modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3F22A801B6DA0D37044386D28A313521"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/S18-1179","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/S18-1179","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ru","key":"innopolis university","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Innopolis University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofia","key":"reznikovapau","last":"Reznikova","name":"Reznikova, Sofia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/s18-1179","pages":"1068-1072","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 12th International Workshop on Semantic Evaluation (SemEval-2018)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122335796"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3f81dc90-5376-4411-931a-3a6f93bc4a6d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"IUCM at SemEval-2018 Task 11: Similar-Topic Texts as a Comprehension Knowledge Source","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382204","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Stance detection is a critical component of rumour and fake news identification. It involves the extraction of the stance a particular author takes related to a given claim, both expressed in text. This paper investigates stance classification for Russian. It introduces a new dataset, RuStance, of Russian tweets and news comments from multiple sources, covering multiple stories, as well as text classification approaches to stance detection as benchmarks over this data in this language. As well as presenting this openly-available dataset, the first of its kind for Russian, the paper presents a baseline for stance prediction in the language.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lozhnikov, Nikita","Derczynski, Leon","Mazzara, Manuel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383207"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU"],"country":["Russia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Innopolis University"],"keyword":["Fake news","Rumour identification","Russian language dataset","Stance Detection","Text classification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stance prediction for russian data and analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84245914/RuStance.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383207","identifier":[{"id":"85064183861","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-83c6230a-8336-4060-868f-73c1a27add1d"],"keyword":["Fake news","Rumour identification","Russian language dataset","Stance detection","Text classification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9CFD650AB7B67BD51FFAA5B5F3C0A5F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84245914/RuStance.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ru","key":"innopolis university","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Innopolis University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikita","key":"lozhnikovpau","last":"Lozhnikov","name":"Lozhnikov, Nikita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","locid":"785a7089-e58e-4aaa-986d-ae0e615ba508","name":"Derczynski, Leon","orcid":"0000-0002-8656-3431","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuel","key":"mazzarapau","last":"Mazzara","name":"Mazzara, Manuel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-14687-0_16","eisbn":["9783030146870"],"isbn":["9783030146863"],"issn":["21945357"],"pages":"176-186","publisher":"Springer","series":"Advances in Intelligent Systems and Computing","status":"p","subtitle":"SEDA 2018","title":"Proceedings of 6th International Conference in Software Engineering for Defence Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064183861"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-83c6230a-8336-4060-868f-73c1a27add1d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stance Prediction for Russian: Data and Analysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383207","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Word clouds have been proven as an effective tool for information access in different domains. As social media is a main driver of large increase in available user generated content, means for accessing information in such content are needed. We study word clouds as a means for information access in social media. Currently-used clouds that are generated from social media data include redundant and misranked entries, harming their utility.We propose a method for generating improved word clouds over social streams. In this method, named entities are detected, disambiguated and aggregated into clusters, which in turn inform cloud construction. We show that word clouds using named entity clusters attain broader coverage and decreased content duplication. Further, an extrinsic evaluation shows improved access to data, with word clouds having grouped named entities being rated more relevant and diverse. Additionally we find word clouds with higher Mean Average Precision (MAP) tend to be more relevant to underlying concepts. Critically, this supports MAP as a tool for predicting cloud quality without needing a human.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Leginus, Martin","Derczynski, Leon","Dolog, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-099599"],"event":{"acronym":"WEBIST","end":"2015-05-22","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2015-05-20","title":"11th International Conference on Web Information Systems and Technologies, WEBIST 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Leginus, Martin"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Social media","User evaluation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entity grouping for accessing social streams via word clouds","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84961762803&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-099599","identifier":[{"id":"84961762803","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000376161300001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-aacdff51-003c-402f-b22c-a36c9af51377"],"keyword":["Recognized named entities","Social media","Social stream access","User evaluation","Word clouds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8C72A3071A7E96FCE48576AFA9517EA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"leginuspau","last":"Leginus","locid":"64d9f58e-9b62-44a3-895b-d1d90558e4a8","name":"Leginus, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","name":"Derczynski, Leon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"dologpau","last":"Dolog","locid":"8dca6359-9ed2-4b65-8bcf-714003a9b1ff","name":"Dolog, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-1842-9131","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-30996-5_1","eisbn":["9783319309965"],"isbn":["9783319309958"],"issn":["18651348"],"pages":"3-24","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","subtitle":"11th International Conference, WEBIST 2015, Lisbon, Portugal, May 20–22, 2015, Revised Selected Papers","title":"Web Information Systems and Technologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961762803"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aacdff51-003c-402f-b22c-a36c9af51377"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Entity grouping for accessing social streams via word clouds","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-099599","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Brown clustering is an established technique, used in hundreds of computational linguistics papers each year, to group word types that have similar distributional information. It is unsupervised and can be used to create powerful word representations for machine learning. Despite its improbable success relative to more complex methods, few have investigated whether Brown clustering has really been applied optimally. In this paper, we present a subtle but profound generalisation of Brown clustering to improve the overall quality by decoupling the number of output classes from the computational active set size. Moreover, the generalisation permits a novel approach to feature selection from Brown clusters: We show that the standard approach of shearing the Brown clustering output tree at arbitrary bitlengths is lossy and that features should be chosen insead by rolling up Generalised Brown hierarchies. The generalisation and corresponding feature generation is more principled, challenging the way Brown clustering is currently understood and applied.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Derczynski, Leon","Chester, Sean"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-208862"],"event":{"acronym":"AAAI","end":"2017-02-17","place":"Phoenix, us","start":"2016-02-12","title":"The Thirtieth AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sheffield"],"keyword":["Clustering","Feature generation","Natural Language Processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generalised brown clustering and roll up feature generation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85007198068","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-208862","identifier":[{"id":"85007198068","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8b6a9549-0895-47d5-8b62-5da549ae0329"],"keyword":["clustering","feature generation","natural language processing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9DE04A68AA6BC0AEBB0BA22ED6B0C94A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leon","key":"derczynskipau","last":"Derczynski","name":"Derczynski, Leon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sean","key":"chesterpau","last":"Chester","locid":"1b7327ba-134e-4ed9-9947-590b6eb9934e","name":"Chester, Sean","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781577357605"],"isbn":["9781577357001"],"pages":"1533-1539","publisher":"AAAI Press","status":"p","subtitle":"AAAI","title":"30th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, AAAI 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85007198068"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8b6a9549-0895-47d5-8b62-5da549ae0329"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Generalised Brown Clustering and Roll-up Feature Generation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-208862","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
